From 9807801291491750e350a391b05d3a27b33274e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:27:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 016/125] route: refuse a direct dial back to the inbound the
 connection came in on

A direct inbound hands out its own listen address as the destination of
what arrives on it. A datagram that the DNS rules did not hijack (a
malformed query, a response, anything else) fell through to the direct
outbound, which sent it back to the same listener, which received it
again: a self-forwarding loop of one session per round, until restart
(1024 sessions, a core and ~90 MB in a minute on a router).

The router refuses a connection whose outbound (a group resolved to the
member it dials through) is direct and whose destination is the listen
address of the same inbound it arrived on; for a listener on every
address, the address the connection was accepted on. The address comes
from the inbound's options (adapter.InboundListenAddress). Chaining to
another local inbound, through a proxy outbound, is untouched.
---
 adapter/inbound.go         |   8 +++
 protocol/direct/inbound.go |  11 +++
 route/route.go             |  55 +++++++++++++++
 route/route_loop_test.go   | 136 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 210 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 route/route_loop_test.go

diff --git a/adapter/inbound.go b/adapter/inbound.go
index ae1067d9a..f3ee22532 100644
--- a/adapter/inbound.go
+++ b/adapter/inbound.go
@@ -21,6 +21,14 @@ type Inbound interface {
 	Tag() string
 }
 
+// InboundListenAddress is implemented by an inbound that gives a connection its own listen
+// address as the destination (a direct inbound without an override, which expects a rule to
+// hijack it). The router uses it to refuse a connection that was not hijacked and would be
+// dialled back to the same inbound, looping without end.
+type InboundListenAddress interface {
+	ListenAddress() M.Socksaddr
+}
+
 type TCPInjectableInbound interface {
 	Inbound
 	ConnectionHandler
